window.docContents[0].resolve({"/Terms/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Terms--Typed-Terms":{"contents":"A cvc5 term.\n\nTyped terms have a type parameter for the actual cvc5-sort of that term. We saw previously that\nToTyp links types to cvc5 sorts, and it is precisely the mechanism used here.\n\nA boolean literal.\n\nBinary conjunction.\n\nAn integer literal.\n\nCvc.lean associates an actual cvc5-sort to these types through the\n\nSome term operators are polymorphic however, addition for instance works on any arithmetic terms as\nlong as they have the same sort.\n\nBinary addition.\n\nNotice that the type-class constraint IsArith α must hold, which asks for a proof that the Typ\nassociated to α is actually arithmetic.\n\nCarries a proof that the Typ associated to α is arithmetic.Proof that α's Typ is arithmetic.\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Terms","header":"3.1. Typed Terms","id":"/Terms/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Terms--Typed-Terms"}});